"""Render synthetic mechanism study from saved results."""
import json
from pathlib import Path

def main():
    root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];out=root/'results'
    d=json.loads((out/'information-experiment.json').read_text())
    html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Pit timing · what can we learn?</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#f5f4ef;color:#182d2b;font:16px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1050px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:32px}.tag{font:12px monospace;letter-spacing:2px;color:#176d62}a{color:#176d62}section{border-top:1px solid #c7d2ca;margin-top:30px;padding-top:12px}.cards{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.card{flex:1;min-width:200px;background:white;padding:20px;border-radius:12px}.number{font-size:34px;font-weight:650}select{font:inherit;padding:9px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}.scroll{overflow:auto}.note{background:#e5eae4;padding:18px;border-radius:8px}svg{width:100%;max-height:260px}</style>
<main><a href="interval-demo.html">← Historical interval test</a><p class="tag">EXPERIMENT 07 · CONTROLLED SYNTHETIC STUDY</p>
<h1>Uncertain lap times do not tell us how much we can learn.</h1><p>All three cases start at the same expected excess lap time (2.04 s) and predictive variance (4.6836 s²). What changes is how much comes from an unknown degradation regime versus fresh observation noise.</p>
<label for="case">Choose the uncertainty split: </label><select id="case"><option value="0">Mostly observation noise</option><option value="1">Intermediate</option><option value="2" selected>More degradation uncertainty</option></select>
<div id="results"></div>
<section><h2>Where does learning change the decision?</h2><p>Each row changes pit loss while keeping this case’s other assumptions fixed. Both policies update after real observations; only the adaptive planner anticipates future updates.</p><div class="scroll" id="sweep"></div></section>
<section><h2>Can we identify the hidden degradation?</h2><p>A separate simulation adds an unknown pace offset that persists across all eight observations. The correct inference model integrates out that offset. This is a recovery diagnostic; the decision planner above still assumes a known baseline.</p><div class="scroll" id="recovery"></div><p>Brier score measures regime-probability error (lower is better; always predicting 50% scores 0.25). Recovery observes all eight laps, even when a policy would have pitted earlier.</p></section>
<section><h2>What this establishes</h2><p class="note">Initial predictive variance alone is insufficient to determine information value. The full predictive distributions differ between cases, and changing regime spread also changes the physical stakes. These are illustrative parameters, not fitted F1 effects. Known-baseline planning gains cannot be transferred to an unknown-baseline setting.</p><p>One optional last stop; known replacement tyre performance; independent Gaussian observation noise; correct regime prior. Numerical optimisation is approximate. No real-race strategy benefit or novelty claim is established.</p><a href="information-experiment.json">Download complete results</a></section><p><a href="nuisance-demo.html">Next: pit decisions with an unknown baseline →</a></p></main>
<script>const d=__DATA__,el=id=>document.getElementById(id),fmt=x=>x.toFixed(3);
function render(){let c=d.cases[+el('case').value],r=c.report;el('results').innerHTML=`<p>Degradation rates: ${fmt(c.scenario.low)} or ${fmt(c.scenario.high)} seconds per lap of tyre age, equally likely.</p><svg viewBox="0 0 900 95" role="img" aria-label="Predictive variance split"><rect x="0" y="10" width="${900*c.learnable_variance/c.total_variance}" height="32" fill="#176d62"/><rect x="${900*c.learnable_variance/c.total_variance}" y="10" width="${900*c.noise_variance/c.total_variance}" height="32" fill="#a6b5ac"/><text x="0" y="75" font-size="18">Unknown regime: ${fmt(c.learnable_variance)} s² · observation noise: ${fmt(c.noise_variance)} s²</text></svg><div class="cards"><div class="card">Expected policy gain<div class="number">${fmt(r.policy_gain)} s</div>Frozen-belief cost minus adaptive cost</div><div class="card">First action<div class="number">${r.adaptive_action}</div>Frozen-belief planner: ${r.frozen_action}</div><div class="card">Rollout estimate<div class="number">${fmt(c.rollout.gain)} s</div>95% paired interval: ${c.rollout.gain_95_ci.map(fmt).join(' to ')} s</div></div><p>30,000 paired simulations. Finer numerical resolution changes estimated gain by ${fmt(Math.abs(c.refined_report.policy_gain-r.policy_gain))} s.</p>`;
el('sweep').innerHTML='<table><tr><th>Pit loss (s)</th><th>Adaptive</th><th>Frozen-belief</th><th>Expected gain (s)</th></tr>'+c.sweep.map(x=>`<tr><td>${x.pit_loss}</td><td>${x.adaptive_action}</td><td>${x.frozen_action}</td><td>${fmt(x.policy_gain)}</td></tr>`).join('')+'</table>';
el('recovery').innerHTML='<table><tr><th>Baseline assumption</th><th>Correct regime after 8 laps</th><th>Brier score</th><th>Brier if offset ignored</th></tr>'+c.recovery.map(x=>{let v=x.by_lap.at(-1);return `<tr><td>${x.offset_sd?'Unknown offset (SD 6 s)':'Known baseline'}</td><td>${(100*v.accuracy).toFixed(2)}%</td><td>${fmt(v.brier)}</td><td>${fmt(v.ignored_offset_brier)}</td></tr>`}).join('')+'</table>';}
el('case').onchange=render;render();</script></html>'''
    (out/'information-demo.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(d)))

if __name__=='__main__':main()
